==Icelandic==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/hauːr/|lang=is}}
* {{rhymes|auːr|lang=is}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|hár|lang=non}}, {{term|hór|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*hauhaz}}.

====Adjective====
{{is-adj|hærri|hæstur}}

# [[high]]
#: [[múr|Múrinn]] er '''hár'''.
#:: The wall is '''high'''
# [[tall]]
#: Guð minn almáttugur! Þú ert orðinn svo '''hár'''!
#:: My god almighty! You've gotten so '''tall'''!

=====Derived terms=====
* [[há-]]

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|hár|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*hērą}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{m|ine-pro|*keres-||rough hair, bristle}}.

====Noun====
{{is-noun|n|hárs|hár}}

# [[hair]]
#: ''Þú hefur [[fallegur|fallegt]] '''hár'''.''
#:: You have [[pretty]] '''hair'''.

=====Declension=====
{{is-decl-noun-n-s|h|á|r}}

=====Derived terms=====
* [[hárgreiðsla]]
* [[hárþurrka]]
* [[í húð og hár]]
* [[skapahár]]
* [[skírnarhár]]

=====Related terms=====
* [[hæra]]

===Etymology 3===
Cognate with the Faroese {{term|háur|lang=fo}}, {{term|hávur|lang=fo}},<ref>{{R:Íslensk orðsifjabók 1989}}</ref> Norwegian {{term|hai|lang=no}} and Swedish {{term|haj|lang=sv}}.

====Noun====
{{is-noun|m}}

# {{context|archaic|lang=is}} a [[dogfish]]{{jump|dogfish|s}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|is|há-}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{jump|s|dogfish}} {{l|is|háfiskur}}, {{l|is|háfur}}

===Anagrams===
* [[hrá#Icelandic|hrá]]

